{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The washers, rubber grommets and 1/4-20 hardware complement supplies I already have: they help spread loads, protect wires through drilled metal and fit my UNC rivet nuts.",
    "The clamp meter extends my inspection and measuring tools into electrical troubleshooting, while small glue tubes offer a convenient option for repairs that do not need mixed epoxy."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The magnetic viewing film has no clear connection to a repair I currently need to make, and exterior wood screws assume an outdoor woodworking project I have not indicated.",
    "The gap-filling glue could be useful eventually, but I have no specific gap repair planned; five rolls of duct tape also feel excessive alongside my existing adhesive tapes."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying tools and repair supplies does not mean every workshop accessory is useful to me right now.",
    "My interest in screws and adhesives seems to have been stretched into more fastening and bonding products without enough attention to their specific purpose or quantity."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatible sizes and practical connections matter: metric washers support my bolt assortments, and 1/4-20 hardware fits the UNC rivet nuts I already own.",
    "My recent purchases point toward drilling, metal fastening and assembly; I prefer supplies that complete those tasks over items that require an unrelated new project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my hands-on repair interests, but the strongest choices filled specific needs around my existing tools and hardware."
}"}
